#question(title: [True or False -- Taylor polynomials])[
  #set text(size: 13pt)

  Let $f$ be a function defined at and near
  $a in RR$. Let $display(n in NN)$.
   \
  Let $P_n$ be the $n$-th Taylor polynomial
  for $f$ at $a$.  \
  Which ones of these are true?

  + $P_n$ is an approximation for $f$ of
    order $n$ near $a$.
  + $f$ is an approximation for $P_n$ of
    order $n$ near $a$.
  + $P_3$ is an approximation for $f$ of
    order $4$ near $a$.
  + $P_4$ is an approximation for $f$ of
    order $3$ near $a$.
  + $display(lim_(x -> a) [f(x) - P_n (x)] = 0)$
  + $display(lim_(x -> a) (f(x) - P_n (x))/((x - a)^n) = 0)$
  + If $x$ is close to $a$, then
    $f(x) = P_n (x)$.

  #v(1fr)
]
